<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="cfa98925">&lt;p&gt;
    Utilizing the matrix, risks should be documented based on frequency, severity and detection. Controls should then be
    evaluated and enhanced to address any residual risk.  A key risk assessment principle is that it should take place
    prior to implementing any changes. Risks should be assessed and control measures and/or mitigating resolution items put
    into action before new work is introduced or systems are changed.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
